Package: curb
Version: 0.1.0
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31)
Recommends: curb-gui
Maintainer: Etienne Gagné-Nadeau <etienne.gagnenadeau@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Etienne-GN/CURB
Description: Per-application bandwidth control for Linux
 CURB (Connection Usage & Rate Balancer) is a NetLimiter-equivalent for
 Linux. It monitors and limits network bandwidth on a per-application basis
 using eBPF, tc/HTB, and cgroups v2.
 .
 Features:
  * Live per-application upload/download rates
  * Per-app bandwidth limits (LAN and/or Internet)
  * Host-wide caps
  * Per-app data quotas (daily/weekly/monthly)
  * Active connection viewer
 .
 Requires Linux kernel >= 5.10 with BTF and CAP_NET_ADMIN (runs as a
 systemd service).
